+# NVFP4 linear operator contract
+
+The experimental PI0.5 `nvfp4_static` route uses `kernels::fp4::fp4_linear`.
+It consumes a contiguous F16 activation matrix `[M,K]` and a packed weight
+matrix `[N,K]`, and returns a contiguous row-major F16 tensor `[M,N]`.
+
+A weight is represented by E2M1 data, swizzled E4M3 scales for each 16 values,
+and one finite positive FP32 `tscale`. Its value is `q * block_scale * tscale`.
+The artifact loader validates shape, block size, scale and buffer sizes, and
+passes `tscale` through `Fp4WeightView`; the operator applies it as cuBLASLt
+alpha. The online activation quantizer currently uses secondary scale 1.
+That activation policy has limited range and is not equivalent to the offline
+weight-only PyTorch simulation.
+
+cuBLASLt computes `W * X^T` as a column-major `[N,M]` matrix. Those bytes are
+exactly the row-major `[M,N]` result expected by Tensor; no output is relabeled
+without a matching layout transformation. The original raw, column-major
+adapter entry point remains available for standalone probes with unit tensor
+scales. Tensor callers explicitly prepare a cached plan with
+`apxinf_fp4_prepare_rowmajor_f16` outside capture, then execute through
+`apxinf_fp4_gemm_rowmajor_prepared_f16`.
+
+The BF16 model route preserves its original numerical sequence: BF16-to-F16
+cast, online activation quantization, scaled FP4 GEMM, F16-to-BF16 cast.
+All five intermediate/output buffers use the active `GraphWorkspace` arena.
+The model reserves the extra per-site bytes (including every action flow
+step) above its BF16 workspace. One persistent 64 MiB GEMM scratch allocation
+belongs to the CUDA context and is reused in stream order. The arena and
+context must outlive graph replay; the existing prepared-plan ownership keeps
+both alive. Normal eager execution still allocates its result tensors.
+
+The adapter caches descriptors and a heuristic-selected algorithm per host
+thread, CUDA device, stream, M/N/K and scratch capacity. Its dtype, layout and
+VEC16 scale mode are fixed by this interface. Resource creation is prohibited
+on an unprepared capture path. Each invocation updates its own scale pointers
+and supplies its tensor-scale product; neither values nor pointers are assumed
+equal merely because two layers have the same shape. Graph replay uses the
+captured CUDA nodes and does not enter the host cache.
+Preparation and capture run on the same host thread in the current synchronous
+runner; plans are thread-local. The map has no eviction until thread exit, so
+long-lived processes repeatedly creating new streams/shapes may retain extra
+library resources. The current gate covers one device/context; it does not
+qualify lower-level calls with mismatched devices or multi-GPU scheduling.
+
+Before each activation-quantization kernel, a stream-ordered clear initializes
+the complete physical scale tile, including row/K padding. This clear is part
+of the captured graph and must also run on replay of a reused/dirty arena.
+
+The maintained composition test uses two non-square shapes, asymmetric signed
+values, zero blocks and non-unit tensor scales (1/32 and 2.5). It compares every
+row-major output element to a CPU dequantized matrix product after F16 rounding.
+It requires no checkpoint or external fixture. From the APXInf checkout:
+
+```bash
+APXINF_CUDA_ARCH=sm_120 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/wheel \
+  cargo test --release -p apxinf-cuda fp4_contract_rowmajor_and_tensor_scale -- --ignored --nocapture
+APXINF_CUDA_ARCH=sm_120 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/wheel \
+  cargo test --release -p apxinf-cuda fp4_graph_replay_bf16_and_distinct_scales -- --ignored --nocapture
+APXINF_CUDA_ARCH=sm_120 CARGO_TARGET_DIR=target/wheel \
+  cargo test --release -p apxinf-cuda fp4_activation_padding_zero_after_capture -- --ignored --nocapture
+```
+
+The second gate captures two equal-shape projections with different secondary
+scales and separate weight-scale buffers after poisoning the arena, then
+changes the same BF16 input allocation and checks every output on four replays,
+including an all-zero input. The third poisons the scale tile on each replay
+and checks every byte for three rows and K=48, including both padding axes.
+Compilation and the pure CPU arena
+size unit test do not establish that this GPU gate passes. After any adapter
+change, rerun all three gates, the full-model `pi05_fp4_graph_smoke` RequireGraph gate,
+and all affected operator/model benchmarks with fresh output identities.
+
+`ModelRunner.execution_mode` only reads the existing implicit plan state
+(`unprepared`, `graph` or `eager`); it does not initialize CUDA resources or
+execute inference. Record it after warmup when reporting native latency.
+
+These gates do not establish GR00T native NVFP4 execution, LoRA residual
+deployment, BF16-model parity, closed-loop success or latency gains. The
+experimental hybrid route retains BF16 weights alongside packed weights and
+still pays online activation quantization and both dtype conversions.
